module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Adjunction.Basic
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Coverage
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.Cech.CoproductRefinement
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# One-member coverings are a reflective subcategory of all coverings

Fix a Grothendieck topology `J` on a category `C` with coproducts, and an object `U`. A
*covering* of `U` is a family of morphisms `{Uᵢ ⟶ U}` whose generated sieve is a covering
sieve, and the refinements between such families make them into a category. Among them sit
the *one-member* coverings `{V ⟶ U}`, which are the same thing as the morphisms `V ⟶ U`
generating a covering sieve.

Sending `𝒰 = {Uᵢ ⟶ U}` to the one-member family `R(𝒰) = {∐ Uᵢ ⟶ U}` is a reflection: the
sieve generated by `∐ Uᵢ ⟶ U` contains the sieve generated by `𝒰`, because each `Uᵢ ⟶ U`
factors through it, so `R(𝒰)` is again a covering; and a refinement `𝒰 ⟶ {V ⟶ U}` is the same
thing as a morphism `∐ Uᵢ ⟶ V` over `U`, by the universal property of the coproduct. Thus `R`
is left adjoint to the inclusion of the one-member coverings, with unit the canonical
refinement `𝒰 ⟶ R(𝒰)` of Stacks 03FI (2).

This is the structure underlying the assertion of Stacks 03P0 — which the source states
without proving it, saying only that a precise lemma will be added "if we ever need it" — that
Čech cohomology of a *sheaf* may be computed from the one-member coverings alone even though
those coverings are not an initial subcategory of all coverings: the one-member coverings are
not cofinal, but they are *reflective*, and a colimit over a category is computed on a
reflective subcategory as soon as the diagram inverts the unit of the reflection. That
assertion is proved in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/Cech/CechCohomologyOfAnObject.lean`, as
`Stacks.CechSite.isColimitWhiskerSingletonCovering`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.CechSite.Covering`: the category of coverings of `U` for `J`, namely the families
  of morphisms with target `U` generating a `J`-covering sieve, with refinements as morphisms.
* `Stacks.CechSite.IsCoveringMorphism`: the property of a morphism `V ⟶ U` that it alone
  generates a covering sieve, so that `Stacks.CechSite.SingletonCovering` is the category of
  one-member coverings of `U`.
* `Stacks.CechSite.singletonCoveringInclusion`: the inclusion of the one-member coverings.
* `Stacks.CechSite.coproductCovering`: the one-member covering `{∐ Uᵢ ⟶ U}` attached to a
  covering, and `Stacks.CechSite.coproductCoveringFunctor` the functor it defines.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CechSite.coproductCoveringAdjunction`: the coproduct functor is left adjoint to the
  inclusion of the one-member coverings.
* `Stacks.CechSite.coproductCoveringAdjunction_unit_app`: the unit of that adjunction is the
  canonical refinement of a covering by the morphism out of the coproduct of its members.

## Implementation notes

A covering is `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.ZeroHypercover` for the precoverage underlying
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.toCoverage`, whose coverings are by definition the
presieves generating a covering sieve. Taking the *generated sieve* rather than membership in
a precoverage is what makes the reflection unconditional: upward closure of a Grothendieck
topology gives `{∐ Uᵢ ⟶ U}` for free, whereas for a precoverage of schemes it is Stacks
03OZ (2), which excludes the Zariski topology.

The one-member coverings are realised as a full subcategory of `CategoryTheory.Over U` rather
than as the full subcategory of coverings with a one-element index type. The two are
equivalent, and the former makes the adjunction bijection literally the universal property of
the coproduct, with no transport along the index equivalence.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03P0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03P0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03FI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03FI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00VT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe w v u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace Stacks.CechSite

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (U : C)

/-- The category of **coverings of `U`** for a Grothendieck topology `J`: families of
morphisms with target `U` whose generated sieve is a `J`-covering sieve, with the refinements
of Stacks 00VT (2) as morphisms. -/
@[sga "4 II 1.2"]
abbrev Covering : Type (max (w + 1) u v) :=
  Precoverage.ZeroHypercover.{w} J.toCoverage.toPrecoverage U

/-- Membership in the precoverage underlying `Covering` is exactly the generated sieve being a
covering sieve.

This is `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff` of Mathlib, and is proved
from it rather than re-derived.  It is kept only as a SPELLING BRIDGE: `Covering` is defined over
`J.toCoverage.toPrecoverage`, Mathlib states its lemma over `GrothendieckTopology.toPrecoverage J`,
and although the two precoverages are equal by `rfl` (checked), `rw` is syntactic and fails to
find its pattern across the two spellings -- deleting this declaration breaks `toCovering` below
with "Did not find an occurrence of the pattern". -/
theorem mem_toPrecoverage_iff {R : Presieve U} :
    R ∈ J.toCoverage.toPrecoverage U ↔ Sieve.generate R ∈ J U :=
  GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff J R

/-- The property of a morphism `V ⟶ U` of **generating a covering sieve** by itself. The full
subcategory it cuts out of `Over U` is the category of one-member coverings of `U`. -/
def IsCoveringMorphism : ObjectProperty (Over U) :=
  fun V ↦ Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton V.hom) ∈ J U

/-- The category of **one-member coverings** `{V ⟶ U}` of `U`, as the full subcategory of
`Over U` on the morphisms generating a covering sieve. -/
abbrev SingletonCovering : Type (max u v) :=
  (IsCoveringMorphism J U).FullSubcategory

variable {J U}

-- The one-member covering attached to a covering morphism, and the one attached to the
-- coproduct of a covering, are built from `PreZeroHypercover.singleton`, whose components are
-- constant in the index.  `rw` and `simp` need that constancy at `implicit` transparency, or
-- else the two sides of a refinement square are not even recognised as composable.
attribute [local implicit_reducible] PreZeroHypercover.singleton

/-- A one-member covering, read as a covering. -/
@[simps toPreZeroHypercover, implicit_reducible]
def SingletonCovering.toCovering (V : SingletonCovering J U) : Covering.{w} J U where
  toPreZeroHypercover := PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{w} V.obj.hom
  mem₀ := by
    rw [mem_toPrecoverage_iff, PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_singleton]
    exact V.property

variable (J U)

/-- The **inclusion of the one-member coverings** into all coverings. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def singletonCoveringInclusion : SingletonCovering J U ⥤ Covering.{w} J U where
  obj V := V.toCovering
  map φ :=
    { s₀ := id
      h₀ := fun _ ↦ φ.hom.left
      w₀ := fun _ ↦ Over.w φ.hom }
  map_id _ := rfl
  map_comp _ _ := rfl

/-- The inclusion sends a one-member covering to itself, read as a covering. -/
@[simp]
theorem singletonCoveringInclusion_obj (V : SingletonCovering J U) :
    (singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).obj V = V.toCovering :=
  rfl

/-- The inclusion sends a morphism of one-member coverings to the refinement whose single
component is the underlying morphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem singletonCoveringInclusion_map_h₀ {V V' : SingletonCovering J U} (φ : V ⟶ V')
    (i : PUnit.{w + 1}) :
    ((singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).map φ).h₀ i = φ.hom.left :=
  rfl

variable {J U}

variable [HasCoproducts.{w} C]

/-- The morphism from the coproduct of the members of a covering **generates a covering
sieve**: every member factors through it, so the sieve it generates contains the sieve
generated by the covering, and a Grothendieck topology is closed under passing to a larger
sieve. -/
theorem isCoveringMorphism_sigmaDesc (E : Covering.{w} J U) :
    IsCoveringMorphism J U (Over.mk (Sigma.desc E.f)) := by
  refine J.superset_covering ((Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).mpr ?_) E.mem₀
  rintro V g ⟨i⟩
  exact ⟨∐ E.X, Sigma.ι E.X i, Sigma.desc E.f, Presieve.singleton_self _, Sigma.ι_comp_desc E.f i⟩

/-- The **one-member covering `{∐ Uᵢ ⟶ U}`** attached to a covering `{Uᵢ ⟶ U}`. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def coproductCovering (E : Covering.{w} J U) : SingletonCovering J U where
  obj := Over.mk (Sigma.desc E.f)
  property := isCoveringMorphism_sigmaDesc E

/-- The source of the one-member covering attached to a covering is the coproduct of its
members. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCovering_obj_left (E : Covering.{w} J U) :
    (coproductCovering E).obj.left = ∐ E.X :=
  rfl

/-- The morphism of the one-member covering attached to a covering is the morphism out of the
coproduct induced by its members. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCovering_obj_hom (E : Covering.{w} J U) :
    (coproductCovering E).obj.hom = Sigma.desc E.f :=
  rfl

/-- The morphism of coproducts induced by a refinement of coverings. -/
def coproductRefinementMap {E E' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') : ∐ E.X ⟶ ∐ E'.X :=
  Sigma.desc fun i ↦ φ.h₀ i ≫ Sigma.ι E'.X (φ.s₀ i)

/-- The morphism of coproducts induced by a refinement restricts on the `i`-th member to the
`i`-th component of the refinement followed by the inclusion of its target member. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem ι_coproductRefinementMap {E E' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') (i : E.I₀) :
    Sigma.ι E.X i ≫ coproductRefinementMap φ = φ.h₀ i ≫ Sigma.ι E'.X (φ.s₀ i) := by
  simp [coproductRefinementMap]

/-- The morphism of coproducts induced by a refinement is a morphism over `U`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem coproductRefinementMap_comp_sigmaDesc {E E' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') :
    coproductRefinementMap φ ≫ Sigma.desc E'.f = Sigma.desc E.f :=
  Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ by simp

/-- The identity refinement induces the identity of the coproduct. -/
theorem coproductRefinementMap_id (E : Covering.{w} J U) :
    coproductRefinementMap (𝟙 E) = 𝟙 (∐ E.X) :=
  Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ by
    rw [ι_coproductRefinementMap, Category.comp_id]
    exact Category.id_comp _

/-- The morphism of coproducts induced by a composite of refinements is the composite of the
induced morphisms. -/
theorem coproductRefinementMap_comp {E E' E'' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') (ψ : E' ⟶ E'') :
    coproductRefinementMap (φ ≫ ψ) =
      coproductRefinementMap φ ≫ coproductRefinementMap ψ :=
  Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ by
    rw [ι_coproductRefinementMap, ← Category.assoc, ι_coproductRefinementMap, Category.assoc,
      ι_coproductRefinementMap]
    exact Category.assoc _ _ _

/-- A refinement of coverings, read as a morphism of the attached one-member coverings. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def coproductCoveringMap {E E' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') :
    coproductCovering E ⟶ coproductCovering E' :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk
    (Over.homMk (coproductRefinementMap φ) (coproductRefinementMap_comp_sigmaDesc φ))

/-- The morphism of one-member coverings attached to a refinement has the induced morphism of
coproducts as underlying morphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCoveringMap_hom_left {E E' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') :
    (coproductCoveringMap φ).hom.left = coproductRefinementMap φ :=
  rfl

variable (J U)

/-- Passing from a covering to the one-member covering by the morphism out of the coproduct of
its members is a **functor**. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def coproductCoveringFunctor : Covering.{w} J U ⥤ SingletonCovering J U where
  obj E := coproductCovering E
  map φ := coproductCoveringMap φ
  map_id E := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
    rw [coproductCoveringMap_hom_left, coproductRefinementMap_id]
    rfl
  map_comp φ ψ := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
    rw [coproductCoveringMap_hom_left, coproductRefinementMap_comp]
    rfl

/-- The coproduct functor sends a covering to its attached one-member covering. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCoveringFunctor_obj (E : Covering.{w} J U) :
    (coproductCoveringFunctor.{w} J U).obj E = coproductCovering E :=
  rfl

/-- The coproduct functor sends a refinement to the attached morphism of one-member
coverings. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCoveringFunctor_map {E E' : Covering.{w} J U} (φ : E ⟶ E') :
    (coproductCoveringFunctor.{w} J U).map φ = coproductCoveringMap φ :=
  rfl

variable {J U}

/-- The morphism out of the coproduct of a covering determined by a refinement of a one-member
covering, by the universal property of the coproduct. -/
def sigmaDescHom {E : Covering.{w} J U} {V : SingletonCovering J U}
    (φ : E ⟶ (singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).obj V) : ∐ E.X ⟶ V.obj.left :=
  Sigma.desc fun i ↦ φ.h₀ i

/-- The morphism out of the coproduct determined by a refinement of a one-member covering
restricts on the `i`-th member to the `i`-th component of the refinement. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem ι_sigmaDescHom {E : Covering.{w} J U} {V : SingletonCovering J U}
    (φ : E ⟶ (singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).obj V) (i : E.I₀) :
    Sigma.ι E.X i ≫ sigmaDescHom φ = φ.h₀ i :=
  Sigma.ι_comp_desc _ i

/-- The morphism out of the coproduct determined by a refinement of a one-member covering is a
morphism over `U`. -/
theorem sigmaDescHom_comp_hom {E : Covering.{w} J U} {V : SingletonCovering J U}
    (φ : E ⟶ (singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).obj V) :
    sigmaDescHom φ ≫ V.obj.hom = Sigma.desc E.f := by
  refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ ?_
  rw [← Category.assoc, ι_sigmaDescHom, Sigma.ι_comp_desc]
  exact φ.w₀ i

/-- The bijection between morphisms `{∐ Uᵢ ⟶ U} ⟶ {V ⟶ U}` of one-member coverings and
refinements `{Uᵢ ⟶ U} ⟶ {V ⟶ U}`: both are families of morphisms `Uᵢ ⟶ V` over `U`, by the
universal property of the coproduct. -/
def coproductCoveringHomEquiv (E : Covering.{w} J U) (V : SingletonCovering J U) :
    ((coproductCoveringFunctor.{w} J U).obj E ⟶ V) ≃
      (E ⟶ (singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).obj V) where
  toFun ψ :=
    { s₀ := fun _ ↦ PUnit.unit
      h₀ := fun i ↦ Sigma.ι E.X i ≫ ψ.hom.left
      w₀ := fun i ↦ by
        rw [Category.assoc]
        exact (congrArg (fun k ↦ Sigma.ι E.X i ≫ k) (Over.w ψ.hom)).trans
          (Sigma.ι_comp_desc E.f i) }
  invFun φ := ObjectProperty.homMk (Over.homMk (sigmaDescHom φ) (sigmaDescHom_comp_hom φ))
  left_inv ψ := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
    refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ ?_
    exact ι_sigmaDescHom _ i
  right_inv φ := by
    refine PreZeroHypercover.Hom.ext' (funext fun i ↦ rfl) fun i ↦ ?_
    simp only [eqToHom_refl, Category.comp_id]
    exact ι_sigmaDescHom φ i

/-- The refinement attached to a morphism `ψ` of one-member coverings has as `i`-th component
the inclusion of the `i`-th member followed by the underlying morphism of `ψ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCoveringHomEquiv_apply_h₀ {E : Covering.{w} J U} {V : SingletonCovering J U}
    (ψ : (coproductCoveringFunctor.{w} J U).obj E ⟶ V) (i : E.I₀) :
    (coproductCoveringHomEquiv E V ψ).h₀ i = Sigma.ι E.X i ≫ ψ.hom.left :=
  rfl

/-- The morphism of one-member coverings attached to a refinement `φ` has underlying morphism
`sigmaDescHom φ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coproductCoveringHomEquiv_symm_apply_hom_left {E : Covering.{w} J U}
    {V : SingletonCovering J U} (φ : E ⟶ (singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U).obj V) :
    ((coproductCoveringHomEquiv E V).symm φ).hom.left = sigmaDescHom φ :=
  rfl

variable (J U)

/-- **The one-member coverings are a reflective subcategory of all coverings**: taking the
morphism out of the coproduct of the members of a covering is left adjoint to the inclusion of
the one-member coverings. -/
def coproductCoveringAdjunction :
    coproductCoveringFunctor.{w} J U ⊣ singletonCoveringInclusion.{w} J U :=
  Adjunction.mkOfHomEquiv
    { homEquiv := coproductCoveringHomEquiv
      homEquiv_naturality_left_symm := fun {E' E V} φ ψ ↦ by
        apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
        apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
        rw [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, Over.comp_left,
          coproductCoveringHomEquiv_symm_apply_hom_left,
          coproductCoveringHomEquiv_symm_apply_hom_left, coproductCoveringFunctor_map,
          coproductCoveringMap_hom_left]
        refine Sigma.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ ?_
        rw [ι_sigmaDescHom, ← Category.assoc, ι_coproductRefinementMap, Category.assoc,
          ι_sigmaDescHom]
        rfl
      homEquiv_naturality_right := fun {E V V'} ψ χ ↦ by
        refine PreZeroHypercover.Hom.ext' (funext fun i ↦ rfl) fun i ↦ ?_
        simp only [eqToHom_refl, Category.comp_id, coproductCoveringHomEquiv_apply_h₀]
        exact (Category.assoc (Sigma.ι E.X i) ψ.hom.left χ.hom.left).symm }

/-- The **unit of the reflection is the canonical refinement** of a covering by the morphism
out of the coproduct of its members, which is Stacks 03FI (2). -/
theorem coproductCoveringAdjunction_unit_app (E : Covering.{w} J U) :
    (coproductCoveringAdjunction.{w} J U).unit.app E =
      PreZeroHypercover.homOverIdEquivHom E.toPreZeroHypercover
        (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{w} (Sigma.desc E.f))
        (coproductRefinement E.toPreZeroHypercover) := by
  refine PreZeroHypercover.Hom.ext' (funext fun i ↦ rfl) fun i ↦ ?_
  simp only [eqToHom_refl, Category.comp_id]
  exact Category.comp_id (Sigma.ι E.X i)

end Stacks.CechSite

end
